(2) order-4 kernels with H(K[A, B]) = Pi_2(A) Pi_2(B) + H(A) H(B) for all |A|, |B| <= 3:
    number of (labelled K, ordered ports) with the Gaussian law on |A| + |B| <= 5: 48
    example: K arcs [(0, 3), (1, 0), (2, 0), (2, 1), (3, 1), (3, 2)], ports (x, y) = (1, 2), H(K) = 5
    checked 2129 pairs (A, B) with |A|, |B| <= 4: law violated 0 times; congruence mod 3 violated 0 times
    |A| + |B| odd: 1188 pairs, 3 | H(K[A, B]) in 1188 of them;  |A| + |B| even: 941 pairs, H != 0 mod 3 in 590
(3) order-5 kernels with H(K[A, B]) = 3 Pi_2(A) Pi_2(B) - H(A) H(B) for all |A| + |B| <= 4:
    number of (labelled K, ordered ports): 480
